                          THE FOLDING OF CLASS TREES

By linking superclass declariations to the superclass which it
references (ie. a doubly linked relationship) the supperclass
has knowledge of its subclasses or siblings.
This knowledge can then be used to support abstractions at a much higher
level.  The superclass can represent the most abstract level or
classification of its data type and have knowledge of its siblings which
respresent more implementational information, thus a general abstraction
can be quirred to find a implentation of the general abstraction that best
fits the need of a specific environment that uses that abstraction.  This
provides a browser for managing the languastical environment a full 
classification scheme.  In an development environment, implementation
descisions based on performance can be pushed off while the development
is in progress by using the top level class abstraction which arbitrarly
chosses one of its offspring as the implementation until a descision can
be made as to what implementation is most efficent.  The tree can be
partitioned or pruned by choising a subset of its siblings that
posses the nessisary capibilities or functions which are called on
the superclass to perform. Not all implementations or subclasses may
support the same capibilities or manipulations.  It is envisioned however
that all subclass will share some capibilities which are
considered to be essentional capibilities of the entire abstract class.

	In the case of marrages between class trees (this
occures when a class inhererts attributes from more than one superclass) the
parents involved will have knowledge of the marrage.  When one of the
parents is queried it can refer to its pardners and to its relationship 
with its class partner based on the offspring that have the parrents in
common.  For example the class of human transportation has many
subclassifications of which cars and trucks are two of them.
Their immediate parrents might be wheeled vehicles.
A class of mamimals might contain horses.  A horse
how ever inherents transportational capibilities thus it has more than
one parrent classification.  If the class mamimals has knowlege of its
marrage with transportation then it can be quired as to what instances
of it support transportation.  This a new classification is implied that
of mamimal transportation.  The marrage knowledge need not be implisit in
the effected parent classes but can be extracted by traversals of the
class nets.  The implied classification also need not be implisit but
rather a consiequence of a marrage.

  The class folding in effect forms a relational data base of procedures
acting on specific data types that is partitioned by data abstraction and
abstraction levels.
